> connect kubectl with created EKS cluster
> install aws cli in t2.large machine
  > sudo apt install unzip 
> also need aws credentials > we already creted it $cat `/.aws/credientials
  > aws configure
> $ aws eks update-kubeconfig --region <region-code> --name <my-cluster>   it will add new context
> kubectl config view
> kubectl config current-context
> kubectl get nodes
> need a service account on kubernetes otherthan default for extra permission like webhook,api etc for that we can create a role and bind it to service account
> here we only need a service account 
> clone the repo to machine > cd kubernetes > ls -ltr 
> kubectl apply -f serviceaccount.yaml
> kubectl get sa
> kubectl apply -f complete-deploy.yaml
> kubectl get pods | wait till everything run
